--------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Purpose & Architecture
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Genotype-to-VCF Pro is an unprivileged, local-first personal genomics
desktop application (PySide6 GUI) and headless CLI converter designed to
transform Direct-to-Consumer (DTC) DNA raw genotype export files (23andMe,
AncestryDNA, MyHeritage, FamilyTreeDNA, tellmeGen) into standardized
VCF 4.2 format with automated GRCh37/GRCh38 build detection and reference
base resolution.

The package is explicitly engineered with the following invariants:
  * Local-First Privacy Boundary (INV-LOCAL-01): Genetic raw data,
    generated VCF files, and local reference indexes remain strictly on the
    local machine and are never transmitted to external cloud systems.
  * Unprivileged User-Space Execution (INV-LOCAL-02): RunAsInvoker non-elevation;
    both GUI and CLI run with regular user privileges without requiring
    administrator or elevated rights.
  * Zero Unsolicited Egress (INV-LOCAL-03): Network communication is strictly
    opt-in and limited to NCBI dbSNP REST queries containing only rsIDs
    (e.g., rs12345) and optional user-selected Ensembl reference downloads.
  * Non-Clinical Research Purpose (INV-LOCAL-04): Software is provided
    exclusively for software engineering and scientific research workflows;
    it is not a medical device under MDR (EU) 2017/745 or IVDR (EU) 2017/746.
  * VCF 4.2 Standard Compliance (INV-LOCAL-05): Strict adherence to VCF 4.2
    specifications with proper handling of autosomal ploidy, pseudoautosomal
    regions (PAR1/PAR2), and sex chromosomes.
  * Tiered Reference Resolution (INV-LOCAL-06): Deterministic reference base
    lookup prioritized across (1) local indexed FASTA, (2) atomic local
    cache (`cache.json`), and (3) NCBI dbSNP REST API.
  * Headless Automation Isolation (INV-LOCAL-07): Robust CLI pipeline
    allowing headless integration in automated bioinformatic workflows.
  * LGPL-3.0 Dynamic Linking Isolation (INV-LOCAL-08): Runtime GUI binding
    via PySide6 utilizes standard dynamic linking to Qt, guaranteeing full
    license isolation and MIT purity for all core application modules.
  * Version Freeze Discipline (INV-LOCAL-09): Strict compliance with policy
    T-20260920-167562623; hygiene and marketing passes never modify the
    application version outside authorized release ceremonies.
  * Statutory Disclaimer & SLA (INV-LOCAL-10): Unpaid open-source donation
    under §§ 516 ff. BGB with liability governed by § 521 BGB; vulnerability
    reports are subject to a 48-hour acknowledgment and 5-day triage SLA.

